course: dictionary
lesson: 9482
title: Steady, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one you need. «Climb only on a steady step stool, never on a chair with wheels.» Here steady means firm and not wobbling, because a safe step must not move under you.
explain: «Porridge, toast, cereal and fruit give steady energy before sport.» Steady does not mean still here. It means even and regular, with no sudden rises or falls. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Steady can also describe a person. «Her steady voice stayed calm when the alarm rang.» A steady voice is calm and sensible, and it shows courage. Steady can also be a verb, as in «Ben put his hand on the wall to steady himself», which means to stop something wobbling.
fact: Steady means firm and not shaking or wobbling, like a steady ladder.
fact: Steady can also mean happening at an even rate, like «a steady speed» or «steady rain».
fact: «Steady» can describe a calm person, as in «a steady voice», and a steady person can be trusted.
fact: As a verb, «steady» means to hold something so it stops moving, and «steadily» is the adverb, as in «the rain fell steadily».
fact: Phrases to know: «steady on!», «slow and steady wins the race», and «ready, steady, go!» for the start of a race.
exercise: «Climb only on a steady step stool, never on a chair with wheels.» What does steady mean here? | Quick and sudden | Very tall | Painted in bright colours | *Firm and not wobbling
exercise: «The horse's gallop soon became a trot, and the trot a steady walk.» What does steady mean here? | Very loud | Very fast | *Even, at the same rate all the time | Sudden and jumpy
exercise: «Her steady voice stayed calm when the alarm rang.» What does steady suggest about her? | *Calm and sensible | Angry and shouting | Hurried and confused | Shaking with fear
test: Ben put his hand on the wall to steady himself. What does steady mean in this sentence? | To hide behind the wall | To run away fast | *To hold something so it stops wobbling | To paint the wall
test: Dad says, «Keep the boat steady!» in a storm. Which meaning fits best? | *Firm and not rocking | Friendly and funny | Very noisy | Happening at a rapid rate
exam: In «a low, steady hum, like a train or a plane engine», what does steady mean? | Very quiet and soft | *Even and constant, never changing suddenly | Coming and going in bursts | Shaking and rattling
